From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 04:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gpu_split: the hang watch names the back's entry, engine and
 wait site

Core patch, next after 0250 (T44). Also applies on mig020-core (T42) and needs nothing from 0233 to
0250. Off unless EDEN_NX2_HANG_WATCH=1.

Runs 182 and 190 froze with "back running (inside a command)" and nothing else: the log gave a word
count that is 4096 words coarse, no method, and no idea whether the back slept or spun. The present
runs on the back (async_presentation off), so its waits for the Vulkan worker and for the display are
the back's waits too, and none of them logs. The hang watch only saw GPU tick waits.

With the switch on, each 5 s report of the front waiting for the back (GpuSplit::Drain and WaitFor)
is followed by:

  Hang watch: the back runs word N of M: <kind> entry, <engine> engine, method, value, last thunk,
              at: <wait site>
  Hang watch: ring at N: ...           the entry and up to 128 words queued behind it, once per place
  Hang watch: texture cache lock S ... state, and who holds it by name
  Hang watch: the GPU is at tick ...   ticks, chunks queued, worker idle or not, submit lock
  Hang watch: worker at: ...; present thread at: ...; fencing at: ...

and, when the GPU has unfinished work, by ReportStall's lines: the unfinished ticks and, on T44, the
ask for the driver's dump (EDEN_NX2_RADV_STALL_DUMP=1). Until now only a tick wait reached those, and
runs 182 and 190 had none, so run 190's stall dump was never asked for. ReportStall's "waited 3 s"
wording stays, because 0250 anchors on those lines; a line before it says it isn't a tick wait.

Wait sites are string literals in one atomic per thread (common/hang_site.h), set by a small RAII
object at each place that can block without a time limit: GetRenderFrame's two waits, the steps of
CopyToSwapchainImpl, RecreateSwapchain and DiscardFrame, the back's WaitWorker in Present, a GPU tick
wait, a pipeline build (ReportRuntimePipeline only logs when it ends), the fencing thread, and a
sleeper on a cache lock (in LockContended, so no lock site changes). "waiting for a cache lock" with
that lock at state 0 is a lost wake-up, the Android freeze of gpu_split.cpp:225 on another atomic.

The report runs on the front, which is stuck anyway: it reads atomics, try-locks and the ring, which
only the front writes, and it lets go of every lock before ReportStall, where the driver's dump can
sleep a second. At most 64 reports. Cost with the switch on: three relaxed stores per ring
entry on the back, and a thread-local read at each marked place. Off, a marked place reads one
thread-local and nothing else changes.

No string of prepare-vulkan-port.py changes its count in these files; of headless/CMakeLists.txt only
two generic ones do ("        }" and "    });\n}"), neither applied to these files. WaitWorker,
DispatchWork and WorkerThread stay untouched: check-vulkan-handoff.py compiles them against its own
mock. Not built, not run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
